    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d925">

                <pb facs="1025" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-12T21:00:00+03:00">October 12, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3913. From Spalding<anchor n="73" xml:id="d925-f1"/> to SPC,<anchor n="74"
                        xml:id="d925-f2"/> Wesson<anchor n="75" xml:id="d925-f3"/> and to the
                    Department for information. General Fleming is returning to the United States
                    after a very successful trip here. He has visited Dnieperstroi,<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d925-f4"/> Stalino and Leningrad and has discussed reconstruction
                    and housing. Suggest that you can obtain valuable and authoritative information
                    from him in connection with lend-lease problems. Soviet authorities especially
                    foreign trade have been most helpful and cooperative in arranging his visit.
                    [Spalding.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d925-f1" n="73" xml:id="d925-f1-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. Sidney P. Spalding, Chief of the Supply Division, United States
                    Military Mission to the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d925-f2" n="74" xml:id="d925-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably the Government Purchasing Commission of the Soviet Union in the United
                    States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d925-f3" n="75" xml:id="d925-f3-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Charles M. Wesson, Director, Division for Soviet Supply, Foreign
                    Economic Administration.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d925-f4" n="76" xml:id="d925-f4-content">
                <p>Dneprostroy was the huge hydro-electrical power station and dam on the Dnepr
                    River near Zaporozhe.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
